<br class="ltx_break"><sup id="id8" class="ltx_sup"><span id="id8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">†</span></sup> Dept. of Electrical Engineering (ISY), Linköping University, Sweden
</span>
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span><math id="m16a" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sharp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">♯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sharp</annotation></semantics></math> Dept. of Mathematics (MAI), Linköping University, Sweden
<br class="ltx_break"><sup id="id9" class="ltx_sup"><span id="id9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">†</span></sup> Dept. of Electrical Engineering (ISY), Linköping University, Sweden
</span>
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span><math id="m18a" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sharp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">♯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sharp</annotation></semantics></math> Dept. of Mathematics (MAI), Linköping University, Sweden
<br class="ltx_break"><sup id="id10" class="ltx_sup"><span id="id10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">†</span></sup> Dept. of Electrical Engineering (ISY), Linköping University, Sweden
</span></span></span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Erik G. Larsson
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span><math id="m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sharp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">♯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sharp</annotation></semantics></math> Dept. of Mathematics (MAI), Linköping University, Sweden
<br class="ltx_break"><sup id="id11" class="ltx_sup"><span id="id11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">†</span></sup> Dept. of Electrical Engineering (ISY), Linköping University, Sweden
</span>
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span>Email: <span id="id12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">chuan.he@liu.se</span>, <span id="id13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">shuyi.ren@liu.se</span>, <span id="id14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">jingwe,marvin.maojw95@gmail.com</span>,
<br class="ltx_break">and <span id="id15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">erik.g.larsson@liu.se</span>
</span></span></span></span></div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, we propose DeMuon, a method for decentralized matrix optimization over a given communication topology. DeMuon incorporates matrix orthogonalization via Newton–Schulz iterations—a technique inherited from its centralized predecessor, Muon—and employs gradient tracking to mitigate heterogeneity among local functions. Under heavy-tailed noise conditions and additional mild assumptions, we establish the iteration complexity of DeMuon for reaching an approximate stochastic stationary point. This complexity result matches the best-known complexity bounds of centralized algorithms in terms of dependence on the target tolerance. To the best of our knowledge, DeMuon is the first direct extension of Muon to decentralized optimization over graphs with provable complexity guarantees. We conduct preliminary numerical experiments on decentralized transformer pretraining over graphs with varying degrees of connectivity. Our numerical results demonstrate a clear margin of improvement of DeMuon over other popular decentralized algorithms across different network topologies.</p>
  
</div>
<div class="ltx_keywords">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_keywords">Index Terms: </h6>Muon, decentralized optimization, transformers, heavy-tailed noise, iteration complexity

</div>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">I </span><span id="S1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Introduction</span></h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A recent matrix-variate optimizer, called Muon <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite>, has garnered widespread attention among deep learning researchers. Muon departs from traditional optimizers, such as Adam <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>, which are based on vectorizing matrix variables, and demonstrates clear advantages through strong empirical results on large-scale, ill-conditioned matrix optimization problems arising in the training of large models. The empirical success of Muon has inspired a large number of research efforts focused on analyzing its convergence <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>, <a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>, <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>, <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>, <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite> and developing its variants, including SWAN <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>, Scion <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>, Gluon <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>, PolarGrad <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>, Dion <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>, and LR-Muon <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite>, among others.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Given the success of Muon in centralized settings, it is natural to ask whether it can be extended to decentralized settings. In this paper, we take a step toward extending Muon to decentralized problems and consider the following finite-sum matrix optimization problem:</p>
<table id="S1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{X\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}}f(X):=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}f_{i}(X)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi mathsize="0.900em">min</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℝ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{X\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}}f(X):=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}f_{i}(X),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where local objective <math id="S1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}:\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}:\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> at each node <math id="S1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, is continuously differentiable and possibly nonconvex, and the <math id="S1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> nodes are connected by a given topology <math id="S1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}=(\mathcal{V},\mathcal{E})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}=(\mathcal{V},\mathcal{E})</annotation></semantics></math>. Here, <math id="S1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}=[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}=[N]</annotation></semantics></math> denotes all node indices and <math id="S1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> collects all directed pairs <math id="S1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)\in[N]\times[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)\in[N]\times[N]</annotation></semantics></math> such that node <math id="S1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> can send information to node <math id="S1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>. In addition, at each node <math id="S1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, only stochastic gradients of <math id="S1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> corrupted by heavy-tailed noise (see Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ I-B Assumptions ‣ I Introduction ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>(c) for details) are accessible. The overarching goal is to solve (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In I Introduction ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) using local computation and peer-to-peer communication, without relying a central coordinator <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>, <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>. Problems in the form of (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In I Introduction ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) encompass a broad range of applications in machine learning and related fields, such as decentralized optimization for neural network training <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>, <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>, matrix factorization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>, PCA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>, low-rank matrix completion <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>, <a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>, <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Despite extensive research on algorithms for decentralized optimization, mainstream approaches—such as DSGD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>, <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite>, Extra <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite>, and gradient tracking methods <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite>—require vectorizing matrix variables when applied to solve problem (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In I Introduction ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). This dominance of vector-variate algorithms in decentralized settings is similar to the situation before the recent success of matrix-variate algorithms in centralized settings. Moreover, research on decentralized stochastic optimization under <span id="S1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">heavy-tailed noise</span> remains limited, with <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>, <a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>, <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>, <a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>, <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>, <a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite> being among the few recent works that address this topic. These limitations in existing works on solving problem (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In I Introduction ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) motivate the following research questions:</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S1.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="122.8" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 122.8" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,122.8) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#0000BF;" fill="#0000BF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 116.9 C 0 120.16 2.64 122.8 5.91 122.8 L 471.47 122.8 C 474.73 122.8 477.38 120.16 477.38 116.9 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2FF;" fill="#F2F2FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 116.9 C 1.97 119.07 3.73 120.84 5.91 120.84 L 471.47 120.84 C 473.65 120.84 475.41 119.07 475.41 116.9 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 85.58)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:1.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:5.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="95.25" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 23.45)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S1.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="S1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="S1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="S1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Can we design a decentralized algorithm that solves problem (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In I Introduction ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) while leveraging the matrix orthogonalization in Muon?</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="S1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Can we further establish its complexity guarantees under heavy-tailed noise conditions?</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="S1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, we address these questions by proposing a novel decentralized variant of Muon, and establish its iteration complexity for finding an approximate stochastic stationary point of (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In I Introduction ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) under heavy-tailed noise regime. Our main contributions are highlighted below.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S1.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We propose a decentralized variant of Muon, named DeMuon, which is the first decentralized optimization method leveraging matrix orthogonalization to solve (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In I Introduction ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). We establish its iteration complexity for finding an <math id="S1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-nuclear norm stationary solution of (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In I Introduction ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) under heavy-tailed noise conditions.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conduct preliminary numerical experiments on decentralized transformer pretraining, and our results demonstrate the superior performance of DeMuon compared to other popular decentralized algorithms across various network topologies.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<section id="S1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S1.SS1.4" class="ltx_text">I-A</span> </span><span id="S1.SS1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Notation</span></h3>

<div id="S1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout this paper, we use <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> to represent the Euclidean space of <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\times n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\times n</annotation></semantics></math> real matrices, and <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the set of all nonnegative integers. We use <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the Euclidean norm of a vector or the spectral norm of a matrix, and <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the nuclear norm and the Frobenius norm of a matrix, respectively. We use <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the trace inner product for matrices.
We define the matrix sign of any nonzero <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{msgn}(M)=UV^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>msgn</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{msgn}(M)=UV^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> are column-orthogonal matrices obtained from the reduced SVD of <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>. For any integer <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we denote <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[N]:=\{1,\ldots,N\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[N]:=\{1,\ldots,N\}</annotation></semantics></math>. For matrices <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, we denote the stacked and average matrices as <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{[N]}:=[X_{1}^{T},\cdots,X_{N}^{T}]^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{[N]}:=[X_{1}^{T},\cdots,X_{N}^{T}]^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{X}:=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}X_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{X}:=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}X_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. We define the stacked local objectives and gradients as</p>
<table id="S1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F(X_{[N]}):=[f_{1}(X_{1}),\ldots,f_{N}(X_{N})]^{T},\hskip 9.24994pt\nabla F(X_{[N]})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi></msup></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="1.097em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F(X_{[N]}):=[f_{1}(X_{1}),\ldots,f_{N}(X_{N})]^{T},\hskip 9.24994pt\nabla F(X_{[N]})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle:=[\nabla f_{1}(X_{1})^{T},\cdots,\nabla f_{N}(X_{N})^{T}]^{T}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=[\nabla f_{1}(X_{1})^{T},\cdots,\nabla f_{N}(X_{N})^{T}]^{T},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and the average local gradients as <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\nabla}F(X_{[N]}):=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\nabla f_{i}(X_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>∇</mo><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\nabla}F(X_{[N]}):=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\nabla f_{i}(X_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.
For any <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\in\mathbb{R}^{p\times q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\in\mathbb{R}^{p\times q}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\otimes B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\otimes B</annotation></semantics></math> denote the Kronecker product of <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>. We present the following useful property of the Kronecker product:</p>
<table id="S1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(A\otimes B)(C\otimes D)=(AC)\otimes(BD)\ \text{holds when $AC$ and $BD$ are defined (i.e., dimensionally compatible).}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">D</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">D</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.460em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em">holds when </mtext><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi></mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em"> and </mtext><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">D</mi></mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em"> are defined (i.e., dimensionally compatible).</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(A\otimes B)(C\otimes D)=(AC)\otimes(BD)\ \text{holds when $AC$ and $BD$ are defined (i.e., dimensionally compatible).}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">For any positive integer <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\times d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\times d</annotation></semantics></math> identity matrix, and <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional all-ones vector. In addition, we use <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the standard big-O notation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S1.SS2.4" class="ltx_text">I-B</span> </span><span id="S1.SS2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assumptions</span></h3>

<div id="S1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now make the following assumptions throughout this paper.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 1</span></span><span id="Thmassumption1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S1.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S1.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="S1.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists a finite </span><math id="S1.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathrm{low}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>low</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathrm{low}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that </span><math id="S1.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(X)\geq f_{\mathrm{low}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>low</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(X)\geq f_{\mathrm{low}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I3.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> holds for all </span><math id="S1.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I3.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="S1.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists some </span><math id="S1.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{*}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{*}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that</span></p>
<table id="S1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\nabla f_{i}(X)-\nabla f_{i}(Y)\|_{*}\leq L_{*}\|X-Y\|\hskip 9.24994pt\forall X,Y\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n},i\in[N]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">Y</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">Y</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="1.097em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Y</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℝ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\nabla f_{i}(X)-\nabla f_{i}(Y)\|_{*}\leq L_{*}\|X-Y\|\hskip 9.24994pt\forall X,Y\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n},i\in[N].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="S1.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exist some </span><math id="S1.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I3.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S1.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(1,2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(1,2]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I3.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that the stochastic estimators </span><math id="S1.I3.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i}:\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}\times\Xi\to\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i}:\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}\times\Xi\to\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I3.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> satisfy</span></p>
<table id="S1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[G_{i}(X;\xi)]=\nabla f_{i}(X),\hskip 9.24994pt\mathbb{E}[\|G_{i}(X;\xi)-\nabla f_{i}(X)\|_{*}^{\alpha}]\leq\sigma^{\alpha}\hskip 9.24994pt\forall X\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n},i\in[N]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">G</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ξ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="1.097em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">G</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ξ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℝ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[G_{i}(X;\xi)]=\nabla f_{i}(X),\hskip 9.24994pt\mathbb{E}[\|G_{i}(X;\xi)-\nabla f_{i}(X)\|_{*}^{\alpha}]\leq\sigma^{\alpha}\hskip 9.24994pt\forall X\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n},i\in[N].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(d)</span> 
<div id="S1.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The mixing matrix </span><math id="S1.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times N}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I3.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> associated with the graph </span><math id="S1.I3.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I3.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> satisfies properties:</span></p>
<ol id="S1.I3.i4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S1.I3.i4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="S1.I3.i4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I3.i4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I3.i4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Primitivity: </span><math id="S1.I3.i4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I3.i4.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and </span><math id="S1.I3.i4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{j}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{j}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I3.i4.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for some positive integer </span><math id="S1.I3.i4.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I3.i4.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I3.i4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="S1.I3.i4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I3.i4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I3.i4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Doubly stochasticity: </span><math id="S1.I3.i4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{N}^{T}W=\mathbf{1}_{N}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>N</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>N</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{N}^{T}W=\mathbf{1}_{N}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I3.i4.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and </span><math id="S1.I3.i4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\mathbf{1}_{N}=\mathbf{1}_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\mathbf{1}_{N}=\mathbf{1}_{N}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I3.i4.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 1</span></span><span id="Thmremark1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(i) It follows from Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ I-B Assumptions ‣ I Introduction ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>(b) that</p>
<table id="S1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(Y)\leq f(X)+\langle\nabla f(X),Y-X\rangle+\frac{L_{*}}{2}\|Y-X\|^{2}\hskip 9.24994pt\forall X,Y\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">Y</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Y</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msub><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Y</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Y</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℝ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(Y)\leq f(X)+\langle\nabla f(X),Y-X\rangle+\frac{L_{*}}{2}\|Y-X\|^{2}\hskip 9.24994pt\forall X,Y\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmremark1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In addition, for convenience, we let <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{F}:=NL_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{F}:=NL_{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, using Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ IV Proof of the Main Results ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>(i) below, we obtain</p>
<table id="S1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\nabla F(U_{[N]})-\nabla F(V_{[N]})\|_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">U</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\nabla F(U_{[N]})-\nabla F(V_{[N]})\|_{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{i=1}^{N}\|\nabla f_{i}(U_{i})-\nabla f_{i}(V_{i})\|_{*}\leq L_{*}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\|U_{i}-V_{i}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">U</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">U</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{i=1}^{N}\|\nabla f_{i}(U_{i})-\nabla f_{i}(V_{i})\|_{*}\leq L_{*}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\|U_{i}-V_{i}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq L_{F}\|U_{[N]}-V_{[N]}\|\hskip 9.24994pt\forall U_{[N]},V_{[N]}\in\mathbb{R}^{(Nm)\times n}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">U</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="1.097em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">U</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq L_{F}\|U_{[N]}-V_{[N]}\|\hskip 9.24994pt\forall U_{[N]},V_{[N]}\in\mathbb{R}^{(Nm)\times n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">(ii) Under Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ I-B Assumptions ‣ I Introduction ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>(d), we define the mixing rate of the mixing matrix <math id="Thmremark1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="S1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda:=\|W-\mathbf{1}_{N}\mathbf{1}_{N}^{T}/N\|&lt;1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">:=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">W</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mn mathsize="0.900em">𝟏</mn><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn mathsize="0.900em">𝟏</mn><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">&lt;</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda:=\|W-\mathbf{1}_{N}\mathbf{1}_{N}^{T}/N\|&lt;1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmremark1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">which characterizes the consensus performance in decentralized optimization (see, e.g., <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>).</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S1.SS3.4" class="ltx_text">I-C</span> </span><span id="S1.SS3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Organization</span></h3>

<div id="S1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The remainder of this paper is organized as follows. In Section <a href="#S2" title="II A Decentralized Muon ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">II</span></a>, we develop a decentralized variant of Muon, referred to as DeMuon. Sections <a href="#S3" title="III Simulation Results ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">III</span></a> and <a href="#S4" title="IV Proof of the Main Results ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV</span></a> present the simulation results and the proof of the consensus error and iteration complexity of DeMuon, respectively.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">II </span><span id="S2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">A Decentralized Muon</span></h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we propose a decentralized variant of Muon, which we call DeMuon for brevity, and establish its consensus error and iteration complexity for computing an approximate stationary solution to (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In I Introduction ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) under heavy-tailed noise.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Our proposed DeMuon generates three sequences, <math id="S2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{M^{k}_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{M^{k}_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{V^{k}_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{V^{k}_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X^{k}_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X^{k}_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, at each iteration <math id="S2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, each local gradient estimator <math id="S2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{k}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{k}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is updated as an exponentially weighted moving average of the stochastic gradients of <math id="S2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> evaluated at <math id="S2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{0}_{i},\ldots,X^{k}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{0}_{i},\ldots,X^{k}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Next, it applies a tracking technique (see, e.g., <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite>) to update <math id="S2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{k}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{k}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, which ensures that <math id="S2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{k}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{k}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, achieve consensus and approximate the global gradient. Then, the local iterate <math id="S2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{k+1}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{k+1}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is updated by aggregating the Muon-type updates with orthogonalization performed on <math id="S2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{k}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{k}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> from neighboring nodes. Details of DeMuon are described in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ II A Decentralized Muon ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.3" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            
          <span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> starting point <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X^{0}_{i}\}_{i\in[N]}\subset\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X^{0}_{i}\}_{i\in[N]}\subset\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}^{0}=X_{j}^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}^{0}=X_{j}^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, mixing matrix <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times N}</annotation></semantics></math>, step size <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, weighting parameter <math id="alg1.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            
          <span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Initialize:</span> <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{-1}_{i}=V_{i}^{-1}=\mathbf{0}_{m\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{-1}_{i}=V_{i}^{-1}=\mathbf{0}_{m\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            
          <span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0,1,2,\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0,1,2,\ldots</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            Update the local gradient estimators: 
<table id="S2.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle M_{i}^{k}=(1-\theta)M_{i}^{k-1}+\theta G(X^{k}_{i};\xi^{k}_{i})\hskip 9.24994pt\forall i\in[N]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ξ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="1.097em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle M_{i}^{k}=(1-\theta)M_{i}^{k-1}+\theta G(X^{k}_{i};\xi^{k}_{i})\hskip 9.24994pt\forall i\in[N].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            Update the global gradient estimators: 
<table id="S2.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{i}^{k}=\sum_{j=1}^{N}w_{ij}(V_{j}^{k-1}+M_{j}^{k}-M_{j}^{k-1})\hskip 9.24994pt\forall i\in[N]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="1.097em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{i}^{k}=\sum_{j=1}^{N}w_{ij}(V_{j}^{k-1}+M_{j}^{k}-M_{j}^{k-1})\hskip 9.24994pt\forall i\in[N].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            Update the local iterates: 
<table id="S2.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{i}^{k+1}=\sum_{j=1}^{N}w_{ij}(X_{j}^{k}-\eta\cdot\mathrm{msgn}(V_{j}^{k}))\hskip 9.24994pt\forall i\in[N]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">η</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">msgn</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="1.097em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{i}^{k+1}=\sum_{j=1}^{N}w_{ij}(X_{j}^{k}-\eta\cdot\mathrm{msgn}(V_{j}^{k}))\hskip 9.24994pt\forall i\in[N].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            
          <span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="S2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The next lemma gives an upper bound on the consensus error of <math id="S2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{i}^{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{i}^{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> generated by DeMuon. Its proof is deferred to Section <a href="#S4" title="IV Proof of the Main Results ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">consensus error</span>)<span id="Thmlemma1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ I-B Assumptions ‣ I Introduction ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> holds. Let <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{i}^{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{i}^{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be generated by Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ II A Decentralized Muon ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> with step size <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> be given in (<a href="#S1.E4" title="In Remark 1. ‣ I-B Assumptions ‣ I Introduction ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>). Then, it holds that <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|X_{[N]}^{k}-\mathbf{1}_{N}\otimes\overline{X}^{k}\|\leq\sqrt{N}\lambda\eta/(1-\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|X_{[N]}^{k}-\mathbf{1}_{N}\otimes\overline{X}^{k}\|\leq\sqrt{N}\lambda\eta/(1-\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 2</span></span><span id="Thmremark2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We observe that the consensus error obtained in Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (consensus error). ‣ II A Decentralized Muon ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> is similar to the one for decentralized normalized vector-variate algorithms; e.g., see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>, Eq.17]</cite>. However, upon closer inspection, the consensus error in DeMuon is measured using the spectral norm, which is always bounded above by the Frobenius norm. Therefore, DeMuon yields a tighter consensus error compared to the decentralized normalized SGD.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The following theorem establishes the iteration complexity of DeMuon. Its proof is deferred to Section <a href="#S4" title="IV Proof of the Main Results ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">iteration complexity</span>)<span id="Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ I-B Assumptions ‣ I Introduction ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> holds. Let <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathrm{low}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>low</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathrm{low}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> be given in Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ I-B Assumptions ‣ I Introduction ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, and <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> be defined in Remark <a href="#Thmremark1" title="Remark 1. ‣ I-B Assumptions ‣ I Introduction ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. Define</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle U_{\mathrm{dm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">U</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">dm</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle U_{\mathrm{dm}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=f(\overline{X}^{0})-f_{\mathrm{low}}+3(N\sigma)^{\alpha}+\frac{2(N+1)\lambda\sigma}{1-\lambda}+\frac{4N\sigma\lambda}{1-\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">low</mi></msub></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi></msup></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=f(\overline{X}^{0})-f_{\mathrm{low}}+3(N\sigma)^{\alpha}+\frac{2(N+1)\lambda\sigma}{1-\lambda}+\frac{4N\sigma\lambda}{1-\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 18.49988pt+3L_{F}^{\alpha}\Big(\frac{2\sqrt{N}\lambda}{1-\lambda}+1\Big)^{\alpha}+\Big(\frac{2\lambda L_{F}}{1-\lambda}+\frac{L_{*}}{2}\Big)\Big(\frac{2\sqrt{N}\lambda}{1-\lambda}+1\Big)+(\alpha-1)\Big(\frac{2\sqrt{\min\{m,n\}}}{\alpha(1-\lambda)}\Big)^{\frac{\alpha}{\alpha-1}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">F</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">F</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msub><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 18.49988pt+3L_{F}^{\alpha}\Big(\frac{2\sqrt{N}\lambda}{1-\lambda}+1\Big)^{\alpha}+\Big(\frac{2\lambda L_{F}}{1-\lambda}+\frac{L_{*}}{2}\Big)\Big(\frac{2\sqrt{N}\lambda}{1-\lambda}+1\Big)+(\alpha-1)\Big(\frac{2\sqrt{\min\{m,n\}}}{\alpha(1-\lambda)}\Big)^{\frac{\alpha}{\alpha-1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{i}^{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{i}^{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be generated by Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ II A Decentralized Muon ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> with inputs <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> given by</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=K^{-\frac{2\alpha-1}{3\alpha-2}},\quad\theta=K^{-\frac{\alpha}{3\alpha-2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=K^{-\frac{2\alpha-1}{3\alpha-2}},\quad\theta=K^{-\frac{\alpha}{3\alpha-2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with some positive integer <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for any <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\|\overline{\nabla}F(X^{\iota_{K}}_{[N]})\|_{*}]\leq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>∇</mo><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\|\overline{\nabla}F(X^{\iota_{K}}_{[N]})\|_{*}]\leq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle K\geq\max\Big\{\Big(\frac{U_{\mathrm{dm}}}{\epsilon}\Big)^{\frac{3\alpha-2}{\alpha-1}},4\Big\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">K</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">≥</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">U</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">dm</mi></msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">4</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle K\geq\max\Big\{\Big(\frac{U_{\mathrm{dm}}}{\epsilon}\Big)^{\frac{3\alpha-2}{\alpha-1}},4\Big\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly drawn from <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0,\ldots,K-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0,\ldots,K-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 3</span></span><span id="Thmremark3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (iteration complexity). ‣ II A Decentralized Muon ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we see that DeMuon finds an <math id="Thmremark3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-nuclear norm stochastic stationary solution of (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In I Introduction ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) within at most <math id="Thmremark3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{-(3\alpha-2)/(\alpha-1)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\epsilon^{-(3\alpha-2)/(\alpha-1)})</annotation></semantics></math> iterations. Approximate stationarity measured by the nuclear norm is a desirable characteristic of Muon-type algorithms; see, e.g., <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>, <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>, <a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>]</cite>. Moreover, this iteration complexity matches the best-known dependence on <math id="Thmremark3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> in the literature of centralized stochastic optimization under heavy-tailed noise (see, e.g., <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>]</cite>). It is possible to further improve the dependence on problem constants (e.g., Lipschitz constants, noise bounds, etc.) in the iteration complexity. However, doing so may require optimally choosing <math id="Thmremark3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\eta,\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\eta,\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> based on these parameters, which we leave as a direction for future research.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">III </span><span id="S3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Simulation Results</span></h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present our preliminary simulation results. We evaluate DeMuon on real-world language modeling tasks. Specifically, we consider a 3M-parameter GPT model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite> and perform an auto-regressive language modeling task on the Multi30k dataset, following the setup in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite>. The model is distributed across <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=8</annotation></semantics></math> nodes connected via three representative network topologies: complete graph, directed exponential graph, and ring graph. We compare DeMuon with three baselines: DSGD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite>, DSGD_Clip <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>]</cite>, and GT_NSGDm <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite>. The training and validation losses are reported in Fig. <a href="#S3.F1" title="Fig. 1 ‣ III Simulation Results ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and Fig. <a href="#S3.F2" title="Fig. 2 ‣ III Simulation Results ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, respectively. The hyperparameters used for the simulations are listed in Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="TABLE I ‣ III Simulation Results ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE I: </span>Summary of parallel update schemes for all competing method and their hyper-parameter selection.</figcaption>
<table id="S3.T1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S3.T1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.T1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm</span></td>
<td id="S3.T1.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.T1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parallel Update Schemes</span></td>
<td id="S3.T1.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.T1.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hyper-Parameters</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T1.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T1.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">DSGD</td>
<td id="S3.T1.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><math id="S3.T1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}^{k+1}=\sum_{j=1}^{N}w_{ij}(X_{j}^{k}-\eta G(X_{j}^{k};\xi_{j}^{k}))\quad i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ξ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}^{k+1}=\sum_{j=1}^{N}w_{ij}(X_{j}^{k}-\eta G(X_{j}^{k};\xi_{j}^{k}))\quad i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S3.T1.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="S3.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=0.01</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T1.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T1.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">DSGD_Clip</td>
<td id="S3.T1.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.T1.1.3.2.1" class="ltx_text"></span><span id="S3.T1.1.3.2.2" class="ltx_text">
<span id="S3.T1.1.3.2.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span id="S3.T1.1.3.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S3.T1.1.3.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left"><math id="S3.T1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{k}=\eta/(k+1),\ \tau_{k}=\tau(k+1)^{2/5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{k}=\eta/(k+1),\ \tau_{k}=\tau(k+1)^{2/5}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="S3.T1.1.3.2.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S3.T1.1.3.2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left"><math id="S3.T1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}^{k+1}=\sum_{j=1}^{N}w_{ij}(X_{j}^{k}-\eta_{t}\text{clip}(G(X_{j}^{k};\xi_{j}^{k}),\tau_{t}))\quad i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>clip</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ξ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}^{k+1}=\sum_{j=1}^{N}w_{ij}(X_{j}^{k}-\eta_{t}\text{clip}(G(X_{j}^{k};\xi_{j}^{k}),\tau_{t}))\quad i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
</span></span><span id="S3.T1.1.3.2.3" class="ltx_text"></span></td>
<td id="S3.T1.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="S3.T1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\eta,\tau)=(10,0.1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\eta,\tau)=(10,0.1)</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T1.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T1.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">GT_NSGDm</td>
<td id="S3.T1.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.T1.1.4.2.1" class="ltx_text"></span><span id="S3.T1.1.4.2.2" class="ltx_text">
<span id="S3.T1.1.4.2.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span id="S3.T1.1.4.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S3.T1.1.4.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left"><math id="S3.T1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{i}^{k}=(1-\theta)M_{i}^{k-1}+\theta G(X^{k}_{i};\xi^{k}_{i})\quad i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{i}^{k}=(1-\theta)M_{i}^{k-1}+\theta G(X^{k}_{i};\xi^{k}_{i})\quad i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="S3.T1.1.4.2.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S3.T1.1.4.2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left"><math id="S3.T1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i}^{k}=\sum_{j=1}^{N}w_{ij}(V_{j}^{k-1}+M_{j}^{k}-M_{j}^{k-1})\quad i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}^{k}=\sum_{j=1}^{N}w_{ij}(V_{j}^{k-1}+M_{j}^{k}-M_{j}^{k-1})\quad i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="S3.T1.1.4.2.2.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S3.T1.1.4.2.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left"><math id="S3.T1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}^{k+1}=\sum_{j=1}^{N}w_{ij}(X_{j}{k}-\eta V_{j}^{k}/\|V_{j}^{k}\|_{F})\quad i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}^{k+1}=\sum_{j=1}^{N}w_{ij}(X_{j}{k}-\eta V_{j}^{k}/\|V_{j}^{k}\|_{F})\quad i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
</span></span><span id="S3.T1.1.4.2.3" class="ltx_text"></span></td>
<td id="S3.T1.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="S3.T1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\eta,\theta)=(0.1,0.2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\eta,\theta)=(0.1,0.2)</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T1.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T1.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b ltx_border_t">DeMuon</td>
<td id="S3.T1.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b ltx_border_t">See steps (<a href="#S2.E5" title="In 4 ‣ Algorithm 1 ‣ II A Decentralized Muon ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>)-(<a href="#S2.E7" title="In 6 ‣ Algorithm 1 ‣ II A Decentralized Muon ‣ DeMuon: A Decentralized Muon for Matrix Optimization over Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>)</td>
<td id="S3.T1.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_t"><math id="S3.T1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\eta,\theta)=(0.1,0.2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\eta,\theta)=(0.1,0.2)</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
